  "causes": [
    {
      "title": "vLLM startup free-memory check fails: device has less free memory than gpu_memory_utilization requires",
      "summary": "The engine refuses to start because free device memory at startup is just below the requested gpu_memory_utilization. Each job then cascades into 'Engine core initialization failed' and server-start failures. The runs are infra-tagged, so ROUTING says rerun as infra. However, the same error hits 109 clusters across 56 agents with no host concentration, on MIG slices that nvidia-smi reports as 0 MiB used. That pattern also fits a systematic increase in torch nightly (cu130) CUDA context/startup memory, which a rerun should rule in or out.",
      "signature": "ValueError: Free memory on device cuda:0 (29.55/32.5 GiB) on startup is less than desired GPU memory utilization (0.92, 29.9 GiB). Decrease GPU memory utilization or reduce GPU memory used by other processes.",
